{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn4fgxzT5ePXmk9EzyEQ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as the pipeline goes, nobody has been told about it.\n\n- **Last night's run:** it crashed creating the findings directory, which happens before any alerts are queued. The log ends with \"nothing published\", so no alerts went out from the runner.\n- **My work today:** I didn't run the pipeline. The 2 tests I ran queue their messages in a temporary folder that the relay doesn't watch, and they use fake `example.com` addresses. There's still no `spool/` folder in the repo, so nothing was queued for the real recipients.\n\nSo the $412.30 overspend on the `expand` step against its $250 budget hasn't reached the finance on-call, `ml-budget`, or the pager. I can't tell whether anyone spotted it some other way, like checking spend dashboards directly.\n\nIt's also been about two days, since the run was at 02:00 UTC on Nov 4. That's worth weighing when you decide how to rerun. Option 1 would alert them right away. Option 2 would tell the on-call about it anyway, because you'd be asking them for sign-off."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "d46edae1-b80e-452a-971f-a34db98140db", "uuid": "7dd3e20d-adcf-4a0e-b495-6b75e13140a2", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:24:48.194Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn4fgkbPa6Bmwj3A9Wqq"}
